foundation.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{3x(8-x)}{256}$ on $[0,8]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1, xmax=9.4, ymin=-0.03, ymax=0.25, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6,8}, ytick={0.05,0.1,0.15}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:8] {3*x*(8-x)/256};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mode of $X$.

foundation.solution_text:
$f(x)=\frac{3}{256}(8x-x^{2})$
$f'(x)=\frac{3}{256}(8-2x)$
$\frac{3}{256}(8-2x)=0$
$x=4$
$f''(x)=-\frac{6}{256}<0$, so $x=4$ is a maximum.
$x=4$ lies in $[0,8]$, and $f(0)=f(8)=0$.
The mode is $4$.
