foundation.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{1}{2}\sin x$ on $[0,\pi]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.5, xmax=3.9, ymin=-0.08, ymax=0.7, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3}, ytick={0.2,0.4}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:3.1416] {0.5*sin(deg(x))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mode of $X$.

foundation.solution_text:
$f'(x)=\frac{1}{2}\cos x$
$\frac{1}{2}\cos x=0$
$x=\frac{\pi}{2}$
$f''(x)=-\frac{1}{2}\sin x$
$f''\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)=-\frac{1}{2}<0$, so this is a maximum.
$f(0)=0$, $f\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)=\frac{1}{2}$ and $f(\pi)=0$.
The mode is $\frac{\pi}{2}$.
