\addplot[thick, domain=2:6] {3*(x-2)*(6-x)/32};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the most likely temperature rise.

development.solution_text:
$f(x)=\frac{3}{32}(-x^{2}+8x-12)$
$f'(x)=\frac{3}{32}(-2x+8)$
$-2x+8=0$
$x=4$
$f''(x)=-\frac{6}{32}<0$, so $x=4$ is a maximum.
$x=4$ lies in $[2,6]$, and $f(2)=f(6)=0$.
The most likely temperature rise is $4$ degrees.
